{
  "summary": "Adds compile-time hardening flags to depends package release builds for Linux and Windows hosts. Specifically, it appends `-U_FORTIFY_SOURCE -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=3` and `-fstack-clash-protection` to `linux_release_CFLAGS`, and `-U_FORTIFY_SOURCE -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=3` to `mingw32_release_CFLAGS`.",
  "problem": "Third-party dependencies built via depends (such as SQLite, ZeroMQ, and Cap'n Proto), as well as internal libraries that do not link against `core_interface` (such as libsecp256k1), only receive `-O2` release flags on Linux and Windows. They miss buffer overflow fortification and stack clash protection unless the toolchain supplies them by default.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author verified that on master using Debian trixie GCC 14.2, no static library in depends invoked checked functions, whereas on this branch `libsqlite3.a`, `libzmq.a`, `libkj.a`, `libkj-async.a`, and `libcapnpc.a` call `_chk` functions (PR description).",
    "Author verified that on Windows cross-builds (`HOST=x86_64-w64-mingw32ucrt`), `libsqlite3.a` calls `__memcpy_chk` (PR description)."
  ],
